  clock: 1  # e8c5
  nonce: e8c5  # e8c5
  data:  # e8c5
    kind: work_item  # e8c5
    title: "python DDG spec supplies no name_for/kind_for, so 0 of 24,915 methods match a ddg_symbols key: the walk runs and its answer is discarded"  # e8c5
    status: todo_hard  # e8c5
    priority: 2  # e8c5
    parent:  # e8c5
    tags:  # e8c5
    - taint  # e8c5
    - adr_0017  # e8c5
    - analysis_quality  # e8c5
    - dataflow  # e8c5
    isbefore: []  # e8c5
    duplicate_of: []  # e8c5
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e8c5
    pr_ref:  # e8c5
    description: "The python LanguageDdgSpec supplies neither `name_for` nor `kind_for`, so every DDG result for a METHOD is stored under a key the taint walk never constructs. The walk runs, the reaching-definitions solve succeeds, and the answer is thrown away at the lookup.\n\nSIBLING OF WI-jopuf, WHICH NAMED THE FAMILY FOR THE WRONG LANGUAGE. WI-jopuf files this defect for TypeScript and prices it P3 for a stated reason: \"TypeScript has 0 catalogued taint sinks, so no amount of TypeScript DDG coverage can move a taint verdict today.\" Python is the inverse -- it carries the richest sink catalogue in the tree -- and the python instance has never been filed. WI-jopuf also states the fix shape: \"extract the kind-slot decision ... and have the spec call it via kind_for, the way go_def_use imports _extract_receiver_type_from_node from go.py.\"\n\nMEASURED, 2026-09-21, both sides built from the same root on this repository:\n\n  analyzer callables                  36,360  (11,445 function + 24,915 method)\n  ddg_symbols                         29,525  kind slot ':function' on ALL\n  analyzer FUNCTIONS matched in ddg     7,912 of 11,445   69.1%\n  analyzer METHODS matched in ddg           0 of 24,915    0.0%\n  methods whose DDG DATA EXISTS\n    under the bare-name/:function key  21,257 of 24,915   85.3%\n\n  taint asks for : python:scripts/measure-factory-receiver-shape.py:138-153:_Scanner._qualified:method\n  ddg stored it  : python:scripts/measure-factory-receiver-shape.py:138-153:_qualified:function\n\nTwo slots differ: the NAME slot (bare vs class-qualified) and the KIND slot. 68.5% of python callables can never have fn_has_ddg true, so every taint finding rooted in one is `unavailable` -> `analysis_method: structural` by construction.\n\nDISCLOSED, AND THE DISCLOSURE UNDERSTATES IT. ddg_build.py's module docstring calls the match \"approximate in one disclosed way ... class context is not walked for Python\". A 0-of-24,915 match is not approximate. Go is named in the same paragraph as the language that does it right, which makes this a cure that shipped wired to one language (the INV-hokig shape).\n\nSECOND, SMALLER MECHANISM, worth fixing in the same pass or filing off: ddg_build.py:279 inserts into ddg_symbols only `if result.ddg_edges:`. A function the solver analyzed and found no dependence in is ABSENT, and absence is read downstream as \"no reaching-definition data was available\" -- absent-versus-empty at the DDG layer. It accounts for part of the 31% of plain functions that also miss.\n\nTHIS IS NOT OBVIOUSLY A PRECISION WIN AND MUST NOT BE SHIPPED AS ONE. Restoring the lookup deletes no findings; it RELABELS them from `structural` to `ddg`/`ddg_mixed`. docs/VERIFY-CLAIMS-SCOPE.md records, measured three times on three populations, that `ddg_mixed` scores BELOW `structural` for precision. Making 21,257 methods walkable could move the number in either direction.\n\nSO THE ACCEPTANCE IS AN A/B, NOT A GREEN TEST. Subject arm against a baseline ledger, every moved situation read at source, in the 0013-0019 pattern, under INV-duvup's pre-registered regime. A pre-registered refutation should be written before the arms are run: if useful precision does not move, the finding is that the walk's verdict was never what made these findings wrong, and that is worth knowing.\n\nFOUND BY: the WI-mojaz diagnosis (2026-09-21), which asked why python test code yields 100% structural findings when python is a def/use language. A Django/unittest test is a method on a TestCase subclass, so that arm is 100% methods, so it is 100% in the 0% bucket."  # e8c5
    fields: {}  # e8c5
