- op: discuss  # f491
  at: '2026-09-22T00:50:53Z'  # f491
  by: agent  # f491
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f491
  clock: 3  # f491
  nonce: f491  # f491
  message: "PREMISE RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-21, and CONFIRMED on a controlled fixture independent\nof the repo-wide count this row was filed on.\n\n24-line probe (two methods + one module-level function, real def-use chains):\n\n  DDG stored          python:flow.py:5-10:handle:function\n                      python:flow.py:12-16:other:function\n                      python:flow.py:19-24:toplevel:function\n  analyzer asks for   python:<abs>/flow.py:5-10:Worker.handle:method\n                      python:<abs>/flow.py:12-16:Worker.other:method\n                      python:<abs>/flow.py:19-24:toplevel:function\n\n  path slot normalised:  FUNCTIONS 1 of 1 match, METHODS 0 of 2\n  name+kind ALSO collapsed: METHODS 2 of 2  -- the DDG data exists for both\n\nSo the filed mechanism reproduces at fixture scale: the NAME slot (bare vs\nclass-qualified) and the KIND slot (:function vs :method) both differ, and the\nwalk's answer is present but unreachable. The first pass of this probe read\n0 of 1 for FUNCTIONS too -- that was an instrument fault of mine (different root\nsemantics in the path slot), not the defect. Recorded so the next reader does not\ncopy a 0 that means something else.\n\nTWO CITATIONS RE-CHECKED IN THE CODE, both exact:\n  - ddg_build.py:279 `if result.ddg_edges:` gates `out.ddg_symbols.add(sym_id)`.\n    NOTE the WI-joluk comment beneath it justifies the gate for\n    `forfeit_refutation`, NOT for ddg_symbols membership -- the conflation of\n    \"analysed, no dependence\" with \"never analysed\" rides along on a rationale\n    written for a different set.\n  - the python spec (ddg_build.py:445) supplies neither hook.\n\nFAMILY ENUMERATED (the row asserts go does it right; here is the whole set).\nFive DDG languages are registered:\n  go          go_def_use.py:310    name_for + kind_for  SUPPLIED\n  rust        rust_def_use.py:363  absent, WITH A WRITTEN REASON at :357 --\n              rust methods are `function_item` nested in `impl_item`, so the\n              defaults are correct. A reasoned absence, not this defect.\n  python      ddg_build.py:445     absent, no reason        <- THIS ROW\n  typescript  ts_def_use.py:316    absent, no reason        <- WI-jopuf\n  javascript  ts_def_use.py:327    absent, no reason        <- FILED NOWHERE\n\nJAVASCRIPT IS AN UNFILED INSTANCE, and WI-jopuf's P3 rationale does not cover it.\nts_def_use.py registers typescript and javascript from the same module with the\nsame `function_node_types=frozenset({\"function_declaration\"})` and no hooks, so\nWI-jopuf's defect is verbatim true of the javascript registration -- but its\ntitle names TypeScript only, and its P3 price rests on \"TypeScript has 0\ncatalogued taint sinks\". WI-nonad (done) records that JAVASCRIPT HAS 83 TAINT\nSINKS. So the javascript instance is mispriced by inheritance from a sibling,\nthe same inversion this row already documents for python. WI-fovus is NOT this\ndefect -- it is the *.js glob question, a different mechanism.\n\nINV-zidur (satisfied) does NOT close the second mechanism here. It added\nTaintFlowFinding.walk_verdict and derives analysis_method from it, which makes\nthe report honest about WHAT THE WALK DID. This row is upstream of that: it is\nabout fn_has_ddg being computed from a set that never contained the function.\nThe two compose -- for a python method fn_has_ddg is always false, so the verdict\nis always \"unavailable\", which is TRUE of the lookup and FALSE of the analysis.\n\nSTILL NOT SHIPPED, and the reason is unchanged: the fix RE-LABELS structural ->\nddg_mixed, and ddg_mixed measures below structural for precision. Needs an A/B\nwith a pre-registered refutation."  # f491
